Code (each file carries the notice in its header):
- bin/vita                  derived from bin/um (the uv launcher), via universal-decompiler's bin/ud
- hooks/add-to-path.sh      derived from hooks/add-to-path.sh (SessionStart PATH hook), via universal-decompiler
- vita_porter/cli.py        derived from um/cli.py (group dispatcher), via ud/cli.py
- vita_porter/common.py     derived from um/common.py (platform and WSL path helpers), via ud/common.py
- vita_porter/kb.py         derived from um/kb.py (knowledge base: sync, search, check, index, new, pr), via ud/kb.py
- vita_porter/publish.py    secret patterns derived from um/publish.py, via ud/publish.py
- tests/test_repo.py        the skill-copy test and the PATH-hook test derived from tests/test_um.py, via universal-decompiler
- tests/test_kb.py          parts of the knowledge-base tests derived from tests/test_um.py, via universal-decompiler

Structure and text (adapted, not copied verbatim):
- hooks/hooks.json, .claude/settings.json, .claude-plugin/, .codex-plugin/, .cursor-plugin/,
  .agents/plugins/marketplace.json, gemini-extension.json, opencode.json, plugin.json: same layout as
  universal-modder's manifests
- AGENTS.md, CLAUDE.md, GEMINI.md, CONTRIBUTING.md, .github/pull_request_template.md: structure adapted
- skills/share-field-notes/SKILL.md: adapted from skills/share-field-notes/SKILL.md
- skills/port-to-vita/SKILL.md: section structure (tools table, the loop, hard rules, references) modelled on
  skills/mod-any-game/SKILL.md (through universal-decompiler's decompile-any-binary)
- knowledge/README.md, knowledge/TEMPLATE.md: structure adapted from knowledge/README.md, knowledge/TEMPLATE.md

From universal-decompiler (same author, MIT), adapted:
- vita_porter/build.py (error-summary patterns, logged runs), vita_porter/proc.py (bounded runs, screenshots,
  exact-PID kills), vita_porter/ps1/WinShot.ps1, vita_porter/tools.py (registry checks), vita_porter/init.py
  (managed .gitignore block, chained pre-push hook), scripts/sync_skills.py, tests/conftest.py (repo fixtures)

Third-party specifications and facts are credited where they're used: hammerill's "LiveArea Specs" gist
(LiveArea layout, with its ya8 colour bug fixed), the VitaSDK headers, vitaGL, Vita3K's command line,
vitacompanion's README, the vita-rust book's memory chapter.
